spec se03-abandoned-fsync-does-not-stall-frontier: 2 sessions, 35 permutations
# SE03, fsync arm. s0 writes s, reserves its commit instant (the WAL commit path's
# allocation, before its fsync) and then abandons it — the fsync-failure path:
# WriteTx.Abandon, then EndVersionedTx. s1 commits x.v = 1 in an explicit Cypher
# transaction. In every interleaving a sessionless read sees s1's commit unless s0's
# reserved instant is below it and not yet abandoned, and no commit is left in
# flight (in_flight_commits = 0) once s0 has abandoned: the abandoned commit does
# not hold the frontier. s's write is never visible.

starting permutation: s0w s0a s0x s0fr s1w s1c s1r
step s0w: lpg: SetNodeProperty(s, v, 1)
step s0a: lpg: Graph.AllocateCommitTS (instant reserved, not published)
step s0x: lpg: WriteTx.Abandon + Session.EndVersionedTx
step s0fr: <MVCCStats: in_flight_commits, sessions_waiting>
in_flight_commits|sessions_waiting
